    grammarFocus: 'Targets: while + past continuous for background actions + suddenly + past simple for the new event · when + past simple for the moment that causes a reaction · no continuous with state and perception verbs (saw, exists) · still + present simple for a situation that continues until now · because of + noun phrase (vs because + clause) · came to + verb for purpose.\nNotice (Activity 1): show the while-sentence. Ask: “Which actions were already happening? Which one is new? Which word warns us that something unexpected is coming?”\nBuild (Activities 2–3): correct was seeing → saw and is still existing → still exists, then build the cause sentence and move “because of this sacred spring” to the front with a comma.\nLikely errors: *When Hagar was seeing this · *is still existing · *because of this spring was sacred · *came for settle.\nUse (Activity 4): five connected sentences about a real place that changed over time (their neighbourhood, a park, a new station), with while, suddenly or when, still, because of and came to; “Meanwhile” can link a second line of events.',
