    grammarFocus: 'Targets: command / tell + person + to + verb for an instruction · will + verb for a role (you will help me) and a promise (I will help you for sure) · sequence of the building: earlier state (was … originally built), change (but … over time), new start (began to construct), completion (After + past simple) · reference words (the old building, on it) · for + noun for who something is for · Over the years · to + verb for purpose.\nNotice (Activity 1): learners sort four parts into “what someone was told to do” / “what someone will do”. Ask: “Who tells whom? Who promises? Which words make the promise stronger?”\nBuild (Activities 2–3): order the five parts about the building and name the word that helped each time, then complete the lines with for / Over the years / to and say why Since and so do not fit.\nLikely errors: *told me do · *I will to help · *After he has built · *Since the years · *spread … for carry the message.\nUse (Activity 4): five connected sentences about a project, tradition or idea that continues after its founder (a school club, a library, a family tradition), with told / asked + person + to, will, after, began to, to + verb and over the years.',
